      "extract": "4. Analysis, and Harmony In §2 we know that if we calculate the Kashaev invariant of the ﬁgure-eight knot only the parameter j contributes. Due to Kashaev [2], the asymptotic behavior of ⟨41⟩N for large N is Z exp \u0014 N 2π√−1 \b −Li2(z) + Li2(z−1) \u0015 dz, where Li2(z) = −R z 0 log(1 −u)/u du is the dilogarithm function. Note that z corresponds to qj and that −Li2(z) and Li2(z−1) corresponds to (q)j and (q−1)j",
